    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan recommends a Hold, and the evidence supports this. AMZN's fundamentals are strong ($84.95B operating cash flow, $201.88B equity, golden cross intact, price 23.5% above 200-day SMA), which argues against selling. However, near-term momentum is deteriorating \u2014 MACD histogram has declined for nine consecutive sessions to its first negative reading since mid-January, RSI has fallen for ten straight sessions from 73.78 to 60.56, price is below the Feb 2 gap open of $171.81, and volume is drying up (relative volume 0.91). With no fresh catalyst on the horizon and risk-reward roughly 1:1 to first support ($164.83) versus 2.9% to the recent high ($174.45), this is not an attractive entry point. Maintaining the position while waiting for either a pullback to the $156-160 zone or a confirmed breakout above $174.45 is the appropriate course of action.\n\n**Stop Loss**: 156.41\n\n**Position Sizing**: Market-weight or slightly below-market-weight allocation; if adding on pullback to $156-160, size at roughly half of what would be deployed at a confirmed breakout\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
